cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use chimorse in your research, please cite this software using these metadata."
title: "chimorse: Symmetry-constrained Fourier–Morse potentials for chiral helix–helix interactions"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ghodrati
    given-names: Hadis
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-1451-8086"
contact:
  - family-names: Kelling
    given-names: Jeffrey
    email: "jeffrey.kelling@physik.tu-chemnitz.de"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1761-2591"
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/hadis-gh/chimorse"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - Python
  - computational physics
  - molecular modeling
  - chirality
  - Morse potential
  - Fourier expansion
  - anisotropic interaction potentials
abstract: >-
  chimorse converts tabulated interaction energies for pairs of chiral helical
  molecules into compact, symmetry-constrained Fourier–Morse potential models.
  It provides data loading, fitting, optional coefficient pruning, model
  evaluation, error analysis, and plotting tools for orientation-dependent
  interaction potentials.
